* ============================================================
* MCC_CORE_SURFACE_AND_INDEX_REGRESSION_V9.DTS
*
* Purpose:
*   Stable split regression for DotTalk++ using two clearly
*   separated phases:
*
*     1) Core surface / non-LMDB behavior on v32 DBF
*     2) Indexed CDX/LMDB behavior on v64 DBF/X64
*
* Design notes:
*   - Do NOT mix v32 and v64 indexed work in the same phase.
*   - v32 phase intentionally stays mostly on natural / classic
*     behavior, with optional INX-style rebuild coverage where the
*     table flavor naturally triggers it.
*   - v64 phase explicitly switches BOTH DBF and INDEXES roots.
*     This is critical. Opening a v64 table while still pointing
*     INDEXES at x32 will make SET INDEX / SET ORDER look in the
*     wrong directory.
*   - Phase 3 is observation-only. It is not meant to prove open
*     area selection after cleanup.
*
* Usage notes:
*   - This script assumes your current public commands remain:
*       INIT
*       SETPATH / SET PATH
*       SCHEMAS OPEN / CLOSE
*       USE
*       SELECT <name>
*       SET INDEX TO <stem|file>
*       SET ORDER TO TAG <tag>
*       BUILDLMDB YES
*   - If the path aliases differ in your build, adjust only the
*     path lines near the top of each phase.
*
* Safety notes:
*   - BUILDLMDB YES is included only in the v64 phase.
*   - Table-buffer and calcwrite probes are reversible.
*   - No PACK / ZAP / DELETE destructive coverage is included.
* ============================================================

SET ECHO OFF
COLOR DEFAULT
ECHO ===== V9 START =====

* ------------------------------------------------------------
* PHASE 0 - INIT / SANITY / PATH BASELINE
* ------------------------------------------------------------
* Goal:
*   Start from a known process state, then observe what INIT and
*   ini files actually set. We do not trust prior session state.
* ------------------------------------------------------------
ECHO ===== PHASE 0 INIT =====
INIT
VERSION
STATUS
WSREPORT

* Optional path echo. Useful when path drift is suspected.
* SET PATH

* ------------------------------------------------------------
* PHASE 1 - CORE SURFACE (v32 only, no CDX/LMDB attach)
* ------------------------------------------------------------
* Goal:
*   Prove the public shell / DBF surface is healthy using the
*   classic v32 data root.
*
* Important:
*   We explicitly close all areas and clear relations first so the
*   phase does not inherit stale open tables or relation state.
*
* Path rule:
*   For this phase we want the DBF root on DBF/X32.
*   We leave INDEXES on x32 as well because any default v32 rebuild
*   or INX activity should resolve there naturally.
* ------------------------------------------------------------
ECHO ===== PHASE 1 CORE SURFACE V32 =====
SCHEMAS CLOSE
REL CLEAR ALL

* Explicit v32 roots.
SETPATH DBF DBF/X32
SETPATH INDEXES INDEXES/X32

* Open the v32 directory into work areas.
* This is the main bring-up for the classic tables.
SCHEMAS OPEN DBF/X32

* -----------------------------
* BUILDING
* -----------------------------
SELECT BUILDING
COUNT
LIST 3
DISPLAY
TOP
SKIP 1
BOTTOM
TOP

* -----------------------------
* ROOMS
* -----------------------------
SELECT ROOMS
COUNT
LIST 3
TUPLE *
TOP
SKIP 1
BOTTOM
TOP

* -----------------------------
* DEPT
* -----------------------------
SELECT DEPT
COUNT
LIST 3
TUPLE *
TOP
SKIP 1
BOTTOM
TOP

* -----------------------------
* MAJORS
* -----------------------------
SELECT MAJORS
COUNT
LIST 3
TUPLE *
TOP
SKIP 1
BOTTOM
TOP

* -----------------------------
* TERMS
* -----------------------------
SELECT TERMS
COUNT
LIST ALL
TUPLE *
TOP
SKIP 1
BOTTOM
TOP

* -----------------------------
* COURSES
* -----------------------------
SELECT COURSES
COUNT
LIST 3
TUPLE *
TOP
SKIP 1
BOTTOM
TOP

* -----------------------------
* TEACHERS
* -----------------------------
SELECT TEACHERS
COUNT
LIST 3
TUPLE *
LOCATE LNAME = "Wilson"
TUPLE *
TOP

* -----------------------------
* CLASSES
* -----------------------------
SELECT CLASSES
COUNT
LIST 3
TUPLE *
TOP
SKIP 1
BOTTOM
TOP

* -----------------------------
* STUDENTS BASELINE
* -----------------------------
SELECT STUDENTS
COUNT
LIST 3
TUPLE *
TOP
RECNO

ECHO ===== PHASE 1 FILTER / LOCATE / COUNT =====
SET FILTER TO
COUNT
COUNT DELETED
COUNT NOT DELETED
COUNT !DELETED
COUNT FOR LNAME = "ANDERSON"
COUNT WHERE GPA > 3.5
COUNT GPA > 3.5

* Filter canary: FNAME = AVA
SET FILTER TO FNAME = "AVA"
COUNT
COUNT FOR GPA > 2.5
COUNT FOR LNAME = "WHITE"
TOP
LIST 10
SET FILTER TO

* Multi-hit LOCATE / CONTINUE canary.
LOCATE LNAME = "ANDERSON"
TUP
CONTINUE
TUP
CONTINUE
TUP
TOP

ECHO ===== PHASE 1 BOOLEAN / SMARTLIST =====
LOCATE LNAME = "Taylor"
LIST 1
BOOLEAN (GPA > 3)
BOOLEAN (GPA < 3)
BOOLEAN (GPA >= 2 AND GPA <= 4)
SMARTLIST 5 FOR GPA >= 3.5
RECNO

ECHO ===== PHASE 1 AGGREGATES =====
SUM GPA
AVERAGE GPA
AVG GPA
MIN GPA
MAX GPA

SET FILTER TO FNAME = "AVA"
COUNT
SUM GPA
AVERAGE GPA
AVG GPA
MIN GPA
MAX GPA
SET FILTER TO

ECHO ===== PHASE 1 DATE/TIME =====
DATE
TODAY
TIME
NOW
DATETIME
CALC DATE()
CALC TODAY()
CALC TIME()
CALC NOW()
CALC DATETIME()
CALC (DATE() = TODAY())
CALC (NOW() = DATETIME())
CALC DATE() + 2
CALC DATE() - 2
CTOD 2000-01-01
CTOD "2000-01-01"
CTOD "2000/01/01"
CTOD 20000101
CALC CTOD("2000-01-01")
CALC DTOC(CTOD("2000-01-01"))
DATEADD 20000101, 30
DATEADD 20000101, -30
DATEDIFF 20000101, 20000103
CALC DATEADD(DATE(), 30)
CALC DATEDIFF(CTOD("2000-01-01"), DATE())

ECHO ===== PHASE 1 TABLE BUFFER =====
* Reversible table-buffer write probe.
SELECT STUDENTS
LOCATE LNAME = "Taylor"
TABLE ON
REPLACE FNAME WITH "DeraldNew"
TUPLE *
LIST 1
COMMIT
LIST 1
REPLACE FNAME WITH "Derald"
COMMIT
TABLE OFF
LIST 1

ECHO ===== PHASE 1 CALCWRITE =====
* Reversible numeric write probe.
SELECT STUDENTS
LOCATE LNAME = "Taylor"
TABLE ON
TUPLE GPA
CALC GPA = GPA + 0.01
TUPLE GPA
COMMIT
LIST 1
CALC GPA = GPA - 0.01
COMMIT
LIST 1
TABLE OFF

ECHO ===== PHASE 1 RELATIONS =====
REL CLEAR ALL
REL ADD STUDENTS ENROLL ON SID
REL ADD ENROLL CLASSES ON CLS_ID
REL LIST
REL REFRESH
REL_LIST
REL_REFRESH

ECHO ===== PHASE 1 SQLITE =====
SQLITE VERSION
SQLITE OPEN :memory:
SQLITE EXEC CREATE TABLE t (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT, n INTEGER);
SQLITE EXEC INSERT INTO t (name, n) VALUES ('alpha', 10);
SQLITE EXEC INSERT INTO t (name, n) VALUES ('bravo', 20);
SQLITE EXEC INSERT INTO t (name, n) VALUES ('charlie', 30);
SQLITE SELECT SELECT id, name, n FROM t ORDER BY id;
SQLITE CLOSE

ECHO ===== PHASE 1 DOTSCRIPT / BLOCKS =====
! echo SET ECHO ON>tmp/mini_regression_v9.dts
! echo ECHO MINI_DOTSCRIPT_V9_OK>>tmp/mini_regression_v9.dts
DOTSCRIPT tmp/mini_regression_v9.dts
SET ECHO OFF
GO TOP

* Branching smoke.
IF .F.
    ECHO IF_BRANCH_RAN_UNEXPECTED
ELSE
    ECHO ELSE_BRANCH_RAN_OK
ENDIF

* Loop buffering smoke.
WHILE .F.
    ECHO WHILE_BODY_RAN_UNEXPECTED
ENDWHILE

UNTIL .T.
    ECHO UNTIL_BODY_RAN_UNEXPECTED
ENDUNTIL

* SCAN on an open v32 table.
SELECT BUILDING
TOP
SCAN
    TUPLE *
ENDSCAN

ECHO ===== PHASE 1 TUPTALK =====
SELECT STUDENTS
TUPTALK RESET
TUPTALK PUSH ALL
TUPTALK PUSH FILTER CND
TUPTALK PUSH 3
TUPTALK PUSH ROW
TUPTALK LIST
TUPTALK NORMALIZE
TUPTALK EXPORT CSV students_norm_v9.csv
TUPTALK EXPORT TSV students_norm_v9.tsv

* Cleanly end the v32 phase before switching roots.
SCHEMAS CLOSE
REL CLEAR ALL

* ------------------------------------------------------------
* PHASE 2 - INDEX / LMDB / CDX (v64 only)
* ------------------------------------------------------------
* Goal:
*   Prove the v64 indexed path using CDX + LMDB.
*
* Critical rule:
*   Switch BOTH DBF and INDEXES roots here.
*   If DBF is x64 but INDEXES remains x32, SET INDEX and SET ORDER
*   will search the wrong tree.
*
* Assumption:
*   The v64 tables live under DBF/X64 and the matching CDX
*   containers live under INDEXES/X64.
* ------------------------------------------------------------
ECHO ===== PHASE 2 INDEXED V64 =====
SETPATH DBF DBF/X64
SETPATH INDEXES INDEXES/X64

* Open a single v64 table for focused index testing.
USE STUDENTS
AREA
STATUS

ECHO ===== PHASE 2 ATTACH / ORDER =====
* Public attach and order workflow.
SET INDEX TO STUDENTS
SET ORDER TO TAG LNAME
AREA
STATUS
TOP
SMARTLIST 10
DISPLAY
TUP

* Secondary tag probe.
SET ORDER TO TAG DOB
AREA
LIST 20

ECHO ===== PHASE 2 SEEK / LOCATE UNDER ORDER =====
* Ordered seek / locate probes.
SET ORDER TO TAG LNAME
TOP
LOCATE LNAME = "ANDERSON"
TUP
CONTINUE
TUP
CONTINUE
TUP

ECHO ===== PHASE 2 REPORTING =====
DBAREA
STATUS
WSREPORT
WSREPORT ALL VERBOSE
SHOW TABLE
SHOW COLUMNS
SHOW INDEX
FIELDS
DISPLAY
TUP

ECHO ===== PHASE 2 KNOWN-SAFE REBUILD (V64 ONLY) =====
* Rebuild the CDX/LMDB backend in the v64 index tree.
BUILDLMDB YES

ECHO ===== PHASE 2 POST-REBUILD VERIFY =====
* Re-attach and verify after rebuild.
SET INDEX TO STUDENTS
SET ORDER TO TAG LNAME
TOP
SMARTLIST 10
STATUS
AREA

* Cleanly close phase 2.
CLOSE
SCHEMAS CLOSE
REL CLEAR ALL

* ------------------------------------------------------------
* PHASE 3 - KNOWN OBSERVATIONS
* ------------------------------------------------------------
* Goal:
*   Record known semantic observations without conflating them with
*   open-area behavior.
*
* Important:
*   Do NOT perform name-based SELECT after cleanup and treat it as
*   a regression. After CLOSE / SCHEMAS CLOSE there are no open
*   areas to bind by name.
* ------------------------------------------------------------
ECHO ===== PHASE 3 KNOWN OBSERVATIONS =====
CALC ((DATE() + 2) > DATE())
CALC ((DATE() - 2) < DATE())
CALC (CTOD("2000-01-01") + 1 = CTOD("2000-01-02"))
CALC (CTOD("2000-01-01") - 1 = CTOD("1999-12-31"))
CALC (DATEDIFF(DATE(), DATE()) = 0)

* Optional reminder only; intentionally commented out because all
* tables are closed at this point, so name-based SELECT is not a
* useful canary here.
* SELECT BUILDING

* ------------------------------------------------------------
* END
* ------------------------------------------------------------
ECHO ===== V9 END =====
QUIT
